From ce05d74efb9768ca8f0ac2529d4026d30b4d7c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 04:06:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] metal: restore upstream's (dk=96, dv=64) sparse-FA shape lost
 in the W1 re-home

Upstream 1e7bcf3da4 (MiniCPM3) added (dk == 96 && dv == 64) to ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_n_kv_max_sparse. W1 60f0a11804 deleted the function and 7fef2f0a05 rebuilt it from the b10819 form, which predates that line, so the union refused the shape for sparse FA while the fa.metal kernels for it survived. Found by the lane-296 Sol-fix dropped-line check (cache/lane296/drop-triage.md). Metal only; the Vulkan build is untouched. Mac compile owed (UNTESTABLE-HERE).

Taken-from: ggml-org/llama.cpp 1e7bcf3da4b2741868d152fa47976fb2501c85e3 (#28599)
Measured-effect: none on this rig (Metal not compiled); restores an upstream shape admit
Conflict-resolved: W1 re-home dropped one upstream line; restored verbatim
Lane: lane-296
---
 ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp
index a413693af7..b1607aacec 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp
@@ -3376,6 +3376,7 @@ static int ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_n_kv_max_sparse(const ggml_tensor * op)
     const bool dk_dv_ok = (dk == 32  && dv == 32)  ||
                           (dk == 64  && dv == 64)  ||
                           (dk == 96  && dv == 96)  ||
+                          (dk == 96  && dv == 64)  ||
                           (dk == 128 && dv == 128) ||
                           (dk == 192 && dv == 128) ||
                           (dk == 192 && dv == 192) ||
